<section class="bg-base-100 py-12 md:py-16">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 md:max-w-5xl">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <%- include('../components/section_title', { text: 'Publication Opportunities', level: "h2" }) %>
    </div>

    <article class="bg-secondary/10 p-4 border border-secondary/20 mb-6">
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-5 border-l-4 border-secondary">
        <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify">Selected high-quality papers presented at AFTMME 2026 will be considered for publication in peer-reviewed proceedings, edited volumes, or journal special issues, subject to editorial approval, peer review, plagiarism screening, publisher policies, and journal/series scope requirements.</p>
        <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify mt-4">Selected full-length papers may be recommended for publication subject to peer review, plagiarism screening, technical quality, publisher approval, formatting compliance, and publication ethics requirements. Acceptance for presentation at the conference does not automatically guarantee publication.</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">


      <article class="bg-secondary/10 p-4 border border-secondary/20 md:col-span-2">
        <div class="bg-base-100 p-5 h-full">
          <h3 class="text-h6 text-secondary font-montserrat font-bold leading-tight mb-4">Discover Materials Topical Collection</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify">Selected high-quality papers presented at AFTMME 2026 may be promoted for possible submission as extended journal articles to the Discover Materials Topical Collection titled “Data-Driven and Advanced Materials for Smart Manufacturing and Energy Applications.”</p>
          <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify mt-4">The Collection focuses on recent advances in sustainable and intelligent materials enabled by advanced manufacturing, data-driven optimization, and artificial intelligence. It covers the design, processing, characterization, and performance optimization of functional, composite, and energy materials for smart manufacturing, renewable energy systems, and Industry 4.0 applications.</p>
          <div class="grid gap-2 mt-5 text-body text-base-content/90">
            <p><strong>Journal:</strong> Discover Materials</p>
            <p><strong>Publisher:</strong> Springer Nature</p>
            <p><strong>Topical Collection:</strong> Data-Driven and Advanced Materials for Smart Manufacturing and Energy Applications</p>
            <p><strong>Guest Editor:</strong> Dr Raman Kumar, Guru Nanak Dev Engineering College, Ludhiana, Punjab, India</p>
            <p><strong>Submission deadline:</strong> 26 December 2026</p>
            <p><strong>Collection link:</strong> <a href="https://link.springer.com/collections/dfcfjihgch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-secondary">https://link.springer.com/collections/dfcfjihgch</a></p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify mt-5"><strong>Important note for authors:</strong> This is only a possible journal publication opportunity. Submission to the Collection is not automatic and does not guarantee acceptance. All manuscripts must be submitted separately to the journal and will be subject to independent editorial assessment, peer review, plagiarism screening, scope suitability, and all standard policies of Discover Materials and Springer Nature.</p>
          <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify mt-4">Conference papers may be considered only if they are not under consideration elsewhere, not already published elsewhere, and not included in any conference proceedings. Authors must ensure originality, copyright compliance, and, where applicable, must clearly declare that the work was presented at AFTMME 2026 and explain how the journal manuscript differs from the conference version.</p>
          <div class="mt-6">
            <a href="/assets/docs/Discover_Materials_Topical_Collection_AFTMME2026.pdf" class="btn btn-secondary">Download Discover Materials Topical Collection Flyer</a>
            <img src="assets/images/Discover_Materials_Topical_Collection_AFTMME2026.jpg" alt="Discover Materials Topical Collection flyer preview" class="mt-5 border border-base-300 w-full h-auto max-w-[450px]">
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="bg-secondary/10 p-4 border border-secondary/20">
        <div class="bg-base-100 p-5 h-full">
          <h3 class="text-h6 text-secondary font-montserrat font-bold leading-tight mb-4">Extended Paper Policy</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify">Authors invited to submit extended versions of conference papers must ensure substantial technical extension beyond the conference version. The extended manuscript should include additional literature review, expanded methodology, deeper analysis, additional results, improved validation, and a clear statement explaining how the journal version differs from the conference paper.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="bg-secondary/10 p-4 border border-secondary/20">
        <div class="bg-base-100 p-5 h-full">
          <h3 class="text-h6 text-secondary font-montserrat font-bold leading-tight mb-4">Journal Special Issue Proposals Under Preparation</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-base-content/90 leading-relaxed text-justify">The organizing committee is exploring journal special issue opportunities based on selected extended versions of high-quality conference papers. Authors of shortlisted papers may be invited to submit substantially extended manuscripts to relevant journals, subject to journal scope, independent peer review, editorial approval, and publication ethics requirements.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>